ation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 199 people. Revenue per employee of $8.6M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $200K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["W. P. Carey Inc. REIT is a large-cap real estate business with a $15.1B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 109% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.092079629306848},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing W.P. Carey (NYSE:WPC) & Broadstone Net Lease (NYSE:BNL)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/reviewing-w-p-carey-nysewpc-broadstone-net-lease-nysebnl.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794597309.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"W.P. Carey Inc. $WPC Stock Bought by Machina Capital S.A.S.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/w-p-carey-inc-wpc-stock-bought-by-machina-capital-s-a-s.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794567577.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"W. P. Carey (WPC) Stock Trades At A Discount To Fair Value","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-wpc/w-p-carey/news/w-p-carey-wpc-stock-trades-at-a-discount-to-fair-value","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794471888.525,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"W. P. Carey (NYSE:WPC) Q3 2026: AFFO Guidance Raised","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/infrastructure-and-real-estate/w-p-carey-nysewpc-q3-2026-a